/// Green-thread runtime controls.
/// @category System
/// Controls over the green-thread runtime the program is already running on.
///
/// `Runtime` is a namespace for runtime-level operations rather than a value: it has no fields and is never
/// constructed, so every member is `static`. `yield` is the first; the type exists so the ones after it are
/// additions rather than a rename.
public type Runtime
	/// Cooperatively reschedule the current green thread.
	///
	/// The next runnable green thread takes over and the caller resumes where it left off once its turn comes
	/// round again — BEHIND everything that was already runnable, never ahead of it. (`main` is the exception
	/// that proves it: it is not a queued green thread at all, so a yield there runs the queued work and comes
	/// back.) If nothing else is runnable the call returns
	/// promptly and the caller simply continues, so a `Runtime.yield()` in a wait loop is a busy wait that
	/// makes progress rather than a block — `await` and `sleep` are the blocking waits.
	///
	/// Unlike `sleep(0)` it occupies no timer, so a program may yield as often as it likes without competing
	/// for the timer store. It is safe outside any async context: called from a program that never spawned a
	/// green thread it simply returns.
	public static function yield()
		__Builtins.yield()
	end 'yield'
end 'Runtime'
